From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:40:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panfrost: don't make image BOs private on panthor

panfrost allocates a resource's BO private to the context's GPU VM (an
"exclusive VM" BO on panthor) unless the resource is created with
PIPE_BIND_SHARED. Panthor refuses to export such a BO: its prime export
returns -EINVAL ("We can't export GEMs that have an exclusive VM").

Any image can be exported long after it was created without
PIPE_BIND_SHARED, though, through EGL_MESA_image_dma_buf_export. That
failure is known: commit "panfrost: Add spec@egl 1.4@egl-ext_egl_image_storage
to the list of failures" (Boris Brezillon, 2023-09-19) records it in the
G52 CI expectations rather than changing the allocation. It now bites real
applications: GTK 4 renders some textures with GL and hands them to its
Vulkan renderer through that extension. On a Mali-G710 (panthor) every such
export failed with "drmPrimeHandleToFD() failed (err=22)", GTK then built a
dmabuf texture with no valid fd, and GNOME Snapshot crashed in
gsk_renderer_render_texture after a photo.

The trade-off: a private BO shares the VM's reservation object, so a job
submission locks one dma_resv for all of them instead of one per BO, and
the BO never needs implicit-sync bookkeeping. That matters most for the
many small, short-lived buffers a frame uses (uniforms, varyings, upload
buffers), which can never be exported. Images, which can, are fewer and
longer lived.

So keep private BOs for buffers, which EGL can't export, and allocate
every image shareable. Reallocating a private image on export instead
would keep the saving for images too, but needs a blit at export time and
a context to do it in, which resource_get_handle doesn't always have.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c
@@ -1164,8 +1164,14 @@ panfrost_resource_create_with_modifier(struct pipe_screen *screen,
        * care to map e.g. FBOs which the CPU probably won't touch */
       uint32_t flags = PAN_BO_DELAY_MMAP;
 
-      /* If the resource is never exported, we can make the BO private. */
-      if (template->bind & PIPE_BIND_SHARED)
+      /* A private BO (exclusive VM) can't be exported: panthor refuses it
+       * with EINVAL. Only buffers that aren't shared stay private: an image
+       * can be exported long after it was created without
+       * PIPE_BIND_SHARED (eglExportDMABUFImageMESA on a GL texture, as GTK
+       * does to hand a GL-rendered texture to its Vulkan renderer).
+       */
+      if ((template->bind & PIPE_BIND_SHARED) ||
+          template->target != PIPE_BUFFER)
          flags |= PAN_BO_SHAREABLE;
 
       char *res_label =
-- 
